  <title>Rotate, flip and straighten</title>
  <p>The buttons in the bottom bar turn the picture left or right by a quarter and flip it horizontally and vertically (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>←</key></keyseq> and <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>→</key></keyseq> turn it). The scan is never changed; the turn is a setting of the frame.</p>
  <p>To straighten a tilted picture, set <gui>Straighten</gui> on the <gui>Conversion</gui> page, in degrees clockwise. The picture is enlarged a little so that it fills the frame and no empty corners show.</p>
  <note><p>The full-quality view (<gui>HQ</gui>) is switched off while a picture is straightened.</p></note>
</page>
